8. Analytical Insights

The project is designed to generate several types of business insights.

Customer Insights

Customer-level analysis can help identify high-value customers and understand differences in transaction activity between customer segments.

Branch Insights

Branch-level analysis can help management compare branches based on deposits, withdrawals, transaction volume, and overall business activity.

Geographic Insights

City and state analysis can identify regions that contribute significantly to banking transaction activity.

Payment Channel Insights

The project compares different payment channels, including:

- UPI
- ATM
- Cheque
- Net Banking
- Cash

This helps understand customer preferences for different transaction methods.

Risk Insights

Credit scores and transaction behavior can be combined to identify customers or transaction patterns requiring additional risk review.

Trend Insights

Monthly, quarterly, and yearly analysis can help identify changes in transaction activity over time.

