12. Real-World Business Applications

Bank Transaction Analytics can be applied to several banking use cases.

Business Performance

Banks can monitor transaction volumes and business contribution across branches and locations.

Customer Management

Customer transaction patterns can be used to understand customer activity and identify valuable customer groups.

Branch Management

Branch-level KPIs can help management monitor operational and business performance.

Risk Management

Transaction behavior and credit information can be used as inputs for risk monitoring and further investigation.

Digital Banking

Payment-channel analysis can help banks understand the adoption of digital and traditional payment methods.

Management Dashboards

The KPIs generated through SQL can be connected to dashboard tools for regular monitoring.

