14. Conclusion

The Bank Transaction Analytics project demonstrates how SQL can be used to transform banking transaction data into meaningful business information.

With more than 100 SQL queries organized into six analytical modules, the project covers the complete analytics process from basic transaction reporting to business KPIs, customer analysis, branch performance, risk analytics, and dashboard preparation.

The project provides practical experience in SQL, business analytics, KPI development, database management, and financial data analysis.

It also provides a strong foundation for extending the project into an interactive Power BI, Excel, or Tableau dashboard.

Overall, the project demonstrates the practical use of SQL for analyzing banking transactions and supporting data-driven business reporting.

